   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "MODEL        TIME   SHOTS  STILL   CHANGE  DREW\nOpus 5.5     n/a    13     0.33 s  17%     approved\nGPT-6 Astra  9 min  15     0 s     22%     \"super bad\"\nGPT-6 Sol    8 min  9      0 s     16%     \"not bad\"\n(Opus figures are for the whole approved video.)\n\nAstra invented compositions that failed in motion:\nbrood in midair over an empty wall, a jumpy camera,\nnear-static weather shots.\nSol stayed in the proven nest set and read clearly.\nAutomatic checks passed both.\n\nAgent mode (shell plus image viewer) beat one-shot\nruns, which gave the rejected single scene.\n\nA segment job: 2 to 4 million input tokens, mostly\ncached, and 15,000 to 25,000 output tokens.\nAstra and Sol share one ChatGPT Codex usage limit;\nthe tests used it up on 19 Oct (back that evening).\n\nGPT-6.1 Sol: not available to Codex on Drew's\nChatGPT account.\nclaude -p works on Drew's Claude plan; never use\n--bare, which switches to API billing.\nSonnet backup: wired and probed once, opt-in only.\n\nPrompting guides: OpenAI's Codex prompting and\nbest-practice pages. Third-party GPT-6 notes are\nunverified.",
   "originalText": "MODEL        TIME   SHOTS  STILL   CHANGE  DREW\nOpus 5.5     n/a    13     0.33 s  17%     approved\nGPT-6 Astra  9 min  15     0 s     22%     \"super bad\"\nGPT-6 Sol    8 min  9      0 s     16%     \"not bad\"\n(Opus figures are for the whole approved video.)\n\nAstra invented compositions that failed in motion:\nbrood in midair over an empty wall, a jumpy camera,\nnear-static weather shots.\nSol stayed in the proven nest set and read clearly.\nAutomatic checks passed both.\n\nAgent mode (shell plus image viewer) beat one-shot\nruns, which gave the rejected single scene.\n\nA segment job: 2 to 4 million input tokens, mostly\ncached, and 15,000 to 25,000 output tokens.\nAstra and Sol share one ChatGPT Codex usage limit;\nthe tests used it up on 19 Oct (back that evening).\n\nGPT-6.1 Sol: not available to Codex on Drew's\nChatGPT account.\nclaude -p works on Drew's Claude plan; never use\n--bare, which switches to API billing.\nSonnet backup: wired and probed once, opt-in only.\n\nPrompting guides: OpenAI's Codex prompting and\nbest-practice pages. Third-party GPT-6 notes are\nunverified.",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
