   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "NOW\nFire-ant video done; its style is the standard.\nToday's runner works when started by hand:\n  make_video.py prepare, then full.\nOpus through the runner: probed, not yet run on a\nfull job. The approved video was made directly.\n\nOUTRO STATUS\nOutro and fire-ant closing: approved, complete.\nFinal fire-ant video: 88.10 s, approved by Drew.\n\nLATER PIECES (not built)\nWire reusable outro into the future automatic runner.\nMusic.\nNew pests need researched drawings first, such\nas a cockroach and a kitchen set.\n\nDREW DECIDED, 19 OCT\nPilot clip only on risky runs.\nDrew picks now, tonight or later when each\nMP3 is approved.\n\nOPEN, FOR DREW\nUsage across many videos on the Claude plan.\n\nDECIDED IN THIS DESIGN\nOpus 5.5 first; Sol, then Astra, when Claude\nusage runs out (Drew, 20 Oct).\nAstra/Sol prompting research: separate, later.\nIdeas adopted: show the target, proven shot types,\nwatch then judge, pilot when risky, learn from\nverdicts. Not adopted: best of two (double usage;\nAstra was \"super bad\").\n\nSTILL UNKNOWN\nWhether GPT-6.1 Sol becomes reachable.\nWhether Astra at ultra beats xhigh.\nWord times are machine-aligned, not checked by ear.",
   "originalText": "NOW\nFire-ant video done; its style is the standard.\nToday's runner works when started by hand:\n  make_video.py prepare, then full.\nOpus through the runner: probed, not yet run on a\nfull job. The approved video was made directly.\n\nOUTRO STATUS\nOutro and fire-ant closing: approved, complete.\nFinal fire-ant video: 88.10 s, approved by Drew.\n\nLATER PIECES (not built)\nWire reusable outro into the future automatic runner.\nMusic.\nNew pests need researched drawings first, such\nas a cockroach and a kitchen set.\n\nDREW DECIDED, 19 OCT\nPilot clip only on risky runs.\nDrew picks now, tonight or later when each\nMP3 is approved.\n\nOPEN, FOR DREW\nUsage across many videos on the Claude plan.\n\nDECIDED IN THIS DESIGN\nOpus 5.5 first; Sol, then Astra, when Claude\nusage runs out (Drew, 20 Oct).\nAstra/Sol prompting research: separate, later.\nIdeas adopted: show the target, proven shot types,\nwatch then judge, pilot when risky, learn from\nverdicts. Not adopted: best of two (double usage;\nAstra was \"super bad\").\n\nSTILL UNKNOWN\nWhether GPT-6.1 Sol becomes reachable.\nWhether Astra at ultra beats xhigh.\nWord times are machine-aligned, not checked by ear.",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
