  {
   "id": "mp_opinion_body",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 5644,
   "y": 7512.5,
   "width": 720.0,
   "height": 120.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#374151",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [
    "mp_opinion_g"
   ],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 209847913,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 115985217,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "1. Check the words for free before Drew listens. The video tool already\n   does it: three offline speech models compare what they hear.\n2. One full take per yes. Fix by re-taking the whole read, never splicing.\n3. Skip voice tests for voices Drew already liked. Chris is ready.\n4. Ask before every take for now. Once trusted: a small cap per episode.\n5. Hand the video step the word timings with the MP3, so it starts at once.",
   "originalText": "1. Check the words for free before Drew listens. The video tool already\n   does it: three offline speech models compare what they hear.\n2. One full take per yes. Fix by re-taking the whole read, never splicing.\n3. Skip voice tests for voices Drew already liked. Chris is ready.\n4. Ask before every take for now. Once trusted: a small cap per episode.\n5. Hand the video step the word timings with the MP3, so it starts at once.",
